      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Competitive little sprint. CAVALRY GIRL (6) is flying this time in and was utterly dominant winning in Adelaide last start, scoring by 4.5 lengths. She drops 4kg off that and should get a nice run tracking a hot speed here, expected to go close again. Like the set up for BAZABALL REWARDED (5) who comes back to her preferred trip of 1000m. She's tried hard in good company her past two but ripped past BEAST MODE (3) over this trip at Sandown Hillside when they clashed. BEAST MODE was first up there but poor last time, his best is good enough but he does need to find it now. ALONG THE RIVER (7) is a ripper. He tried hard again to 1100m last time but is far better suited back to his pet trip. STOKKE (2) resumes. She's a sharp mare who loves this trip and should go well with Shinn on.",
